                                                           )


ORDER ON CORRECTED AND UPDATED JOINT MOTION OF EL PASO ELECTRIC
COMPANY AND NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION ADVISORY
    STAFF TO MODIFY PROCEDURAL ORDER, VACATE DEADLINES AND
      ESTABLISH PROCEDURES FOR CONSIDERING A STIPULATION

       THIS MATTER comes before the Hearing Examiners upon the Corrected and

Updated Joint Motion of El Paso Electric Company (“EPE”) and New Mexico Public

Regulation Commission Advisory Staff (“Staff”) to Modify Procedural Order, Vacate

Deadlines and Establish Procedures for Considering a Stipulation (“Motion”) filed October

20, 2026. Being duly informed, the Hearing Examiners FIND and CONCLUDE:

       1.      On August 27, 2026, the Hearing Examiners issued their Order Establishing

Revised Procedural Schedule and Addressing Outstanding Motions establishing the following

procedural deadlines:

            a. October 23, 2026: deadline for Staff and Intervenors to file direct testimony;

            b. November 20, 2026: deadline to file rebuttal testimony;

            c. December 3, 2026: deadline to file a stipulation; and

            d. December 9 - 22, 2026: public hearing.

       2.      This Motion was filed by EPE and Staff collectively (“Joint Movants”) on

Tuesday, October 20, 2026, prior to the Friday, October 23, 2026, deadline for Staff and

Intervenor direct testimony.
             BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Order on Motion to Modify Procedural Order and Vacate Deadlines Docket No. 25-00082-UT


             3.      The following parties opposed the motion: Coalition for Clean Affordable

Energy, Doña Ana County, New Mexico Department of Justice, Dwight Eggers, and Stephen

Fischmann.1

             4.      Doña Ana County also responded in opposition by stating “[t]he County

opposes the relief requested and does not believe it is realistic or wise to have a dispute over

the schedule 3 days before the critical testimony deadline.”

             5.      This Motion has five parties opposed and only allows for a very limited amount

of time for any response to the Motion to be filed. Therefore, the Motion to vacate the

testimony deadlines is not well taken.

             POTENTIAL STIPULATION DEADLINES

             6.      Joint Movants are requesting the following stipulation schedule:

                  a. Status Conference, before October 30;

                  b. Deadline for Filing a Stipulation and Testimony in Support, [Sunday] November

                     15;

                  c. Deadline to File Statements Opposing the Stipulation and Testimony in

                     opposition to the Stipulation, [Friday] November 20;

                  d. Deadline to File Stipulation Rebuttal Testimony, [Friday] November 30.2

             7.      The proposed schedule only allows four (4) days for the filing of a statement of

opposition and opposition testimony.




   1
       Motion at 3.
   2
       Id.

                                                   -2-
             BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Order on Motion to Modify Procedural Order and Vacate Deadlines Docket No. 25-00082-UT


        8.      If the parties wish to file a stipulation, the Hearing Examiners recommend the

parties work to follow the following timeframe, if possible:

             a. Stipulation filed by Wednesday, November 4th.

             b. Statements in Opposition to the stipulation, Monday, October 9th.

             c. Testimony in support of stipulation, Wednesday, November 11th.

             d. Testimony in opposition to the stipulation, Monday, November 23rd.

             e. Rebuttal to stipulation testimony, Wednesday, December 2nd.

        9.      Parties are encouraged to file if some issues in the proceeding can be resolved

through a non-comprehensive stipulation.

       IT IS THEREFORE ORDERED:

       A.       The Motion to Modify Procedural Order, Vacate Deadlines and Establish

Procedures for Considering a Stipulation is DENIED.

       B.       The testimony deadlines of October 23, 2026 and November 20, 2026

will remain as scheduled.

       C.       If a stipulation is filed, an order setting deadlines will be issued.

ISSUED under the Seal of the Commission at Santa Fe, New Mexico, on October 21, 2026.

                       NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION



